        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9ae2dec7-66c2-5175-a58c-9dd8b29d50b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ken Kwapis, John Woo, Chow Yun-fat\n- Roles: film director, television director, screenwriter, filmmaker, actor\n- Films: Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird, Vibes, The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants, He's Just Not That into You, A Better Tomorrow, The Killer, Hard Boiled, Red Cliff, Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon\n- Concepts: single-camera sitcom, heroic bloodshed\n\nFacts:\n- Ken Kwapis was born on August 17, 1957, and he is an American film and television director and screenwriter.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird in 1985.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the film Vibes.\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film A Better Tomorrow in 1986.\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film The Killer in 1989.\n- Ken Kwapis specialized in the single-camera sitcom in the 1990s and 2000s.\n- John Woo directed the Hong Kong action film Hard Boiled in 1992.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants in 2005.\n- John Woo directed Red Cliff in 2008 and 2009.\n- Ken Kwapis directed the feature film He's Just Not That into You in 2009.\n- Chow Yun-fat is best known in Asia for collaborating with filmmaker John Woo in the heroic bloodshed films A Better Tomorrow, The Killer, and Hard Boiled.\n- Chow Yun-fat is best known in the West for playing Li Mu-bai in Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "59fa4652-869f-5e9f-b336-da2db86c5659",
        "text": "Page: Ken Kwapis. Sentence: Kenneth William \"Ken\" Kwapis (born August 17, 1957) is an American film and television director and screenwriter.\nPage: Ken Kwapis. Sentence: He specialized in the single-camera sitcom in the 1990s and 2000s and has directed feature films such as \"Sesame Street Presents Follow That Bird\" (1985), \"The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants\" (2005), and \"He's Just Not That into You\" (2009).\nPage: John Woo. Sentence: Woo has directed several notable Hong Kong action films, among them, \"A Better Tomorrow\" (1986), \"The Killer\" (1989), \"Hard Boiled\" (1992), and \"Red Cliff\" (2008/2009).\nPage: Vibes (film). Sentence: It was directed by Ken Kwapis.\nPage: Chow Yun-fat. Sentence: He is best known in Asia for his collaborations with filmmaker John Woo in the heroic bloodshed-genre films \"A Better Tomorrow\", \"The Killer\" and \"Hard Boiled\"; and in the West for his roles as Li Mu-bai in \"Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon\" and Sao Feng in \"\".",
